# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RLS integration test configuration (committed TEMPLATE — placeholders only)
#
# Copy this file to `.env.test.local` and fill in REAL values, then run:
#     npm run test:rls
#
# `.env.test.local` is gitignored (the `*.local` rule), so your real
# credentials and seeded ids never get committed. This `.example` file is the
# only one tracked by git. See SETUP.md section 7 for how to create the
# accounts and seed the absence fixtures.
#
# These values are read from process.env by src/__tests__/rls.integration.test.ts.
# If the base block is incomplete the whole suite skips with a reason; if the
# extension (0003) block is incomplete only the 0003 cases skip.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Base role-escalation suite (required to run anything) ------------------
RLS_TEST_SUPABASE_URL=https://tfhhwqmnhrcjefeafzot.supabase.co
RLS_TEST_ANON_KEY=<your anon public key — the VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY from .env>

# A seeded account whose role is 'member'
RLS_TEST_MEMBER_EMAIL=<member1@example.com>
RLS_TEST_MEMBER_PASSWORD=<...>

# A seeded account whose role is 'officer' (promote via SETUP.md section 4)
RLS_TEST_OFFICER_EMAIL=<officer@example.com>
RLS_TEST_OFFICER_PASSWORD=<...>

# A THIRD profile id the officer may promote/demote and whose theme the officer
# must NOT be able to overwrite. The second member's profile id works here.
RLS_TEST_TARGET_PROFILE_ID=<a third profile uuid>

# --- Extension (0003/0004) suite — absences / reviewers --------------------
# A SECOND member account (to prove one member cannot read another's absence data)
RLS_TEST_MEMBER2_EMAIL=<member2@example.com>
RLS_TEST_MEMBER2_PASSWORD=<...>

# A PENDING absence_requests id owned by the FIRST member (ideally carrying an
# evidence_url). File one request through the app as member1, optionally with an
# evidence link, then read the id from the SQL editor.
RLS_TEST_ABSENCE_REQUEST_ID=<pending absence_requests uuid owned by member1>
